    {
      "params": {
        "field": "terminal designators",
        "reason": "Coilcraft does not number the terminals. The marking bar identifies the start lead, so it is the natural pin 1; the inductor itself is not polarised.",
        "source": "https://www.coilcraft.com/getmedia/50632d43-da1b-4cdb-8ab4-3029cab51df3/xfl4020.pdf (745-3 top-view callout)",
        "value": "pin 1 = start (short) lead terminal under the marking bar; pin 2 = the other terminal"
      },
      "type": "assumption"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "field": "CAD package dimensions",
        "reason": "The drawing dimensions the body, terminal width, gap, length and thickness; it draws but does not dimension the corner radius, the terminal setback (taken as symmetric) and the bar, which are scaled from the drawing so the representative model has single values. The model uses the maximum height so clearance checks are conservative.",
        "source": "https://www.coilcraft.com/getmedia/50632d43-da1b-4cdb-8ab4-3029cab51df3/xfl4020.pdf (745-3)",
        "value": "nominal 4.0 x 4.0 body at the 2.10 maximum height; terminals 0.82 x 3.25 x 0.10 below the moulded body, centred in Y and symmetric in X (outer edges 0.395 from the body ends); body corner radius 0.2; marking bar 0.15 x 2.4, 0.5 from the start-lead end, recessed 0.02; pin 1 at -X"
      },
      "type": "assumption"
    },
    {
      "params": {
        "field": "manufacturer CAD",
        "note": "No redistributable model found. The product page's 3D Model button links a free XFL4020 series STEP on coilcraft.com (no account) and a 3D ContentCentral copy (account); neither states a licence, and coilcraft.com answers scripted requests with a Cloudflare challenge, so the STEP is recorded as a link in terms.json (distribution unknown), not stored. SnapMagic (SnapEDA) and SamacSys list models behind accounts. KiCad's L_Coilcraft_XxL4020 footprint names a model file that kicad-packages3D lacks; its XAL4020 model (a 4.3 x 4.3 x 2.1 mm block, CC-BY-SA-4.0) is kept under artifacts/cad/vendor/ as evidence. Geometry is generated from the data sheet drawing (library/cad/py/catalog/coilcraft-xfl4020-152me.py).",
